From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:13:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] esp32-pixelcast board build: MoonLight next to
 esp32-pixelcast

sdkconfig.defaults.pixelcast builds MoonLight for the board of
esp32-pixelcast (https://github.com/spolack/esp32-pixelcast), in one app
slot of its 4 MB dual-boot table (partitions/pixelcast_4mb.csv, WLED's
layout): classic ESP32, WiFi, W5500 Ethernet on SPI, GPIO 25 (the output
enable of the 74HCT245 in front of the LED outputs) driven low at start
(CONFIG_MM_PIXELCAST, esp32/main/pixelcast.cpp).

To fit the 1.5 MB slot: -Os, silent asserts, errors-only log, no IPv6, no
HTTPS (updates over plain HTTP or by upload), no WiFi enterprise, OWE or
SAE on the access point, only the P-256 curve (WPA3-Personal's), no mDNS
browse or console, the logo at 64 px (shown at 28). WPA2 and WPA3-Personal
stay. 1.53 MB with the OLED (patch 6).

1 ms FreeRTOS ticks (frame and lock waits, the HTTP server ticked from the
render loop), lwIP on core 0, larger lwIP mailboxes and TCP window: an
upload next to a stream of universes.

  idf.py -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.pixelcast" build
